#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063990 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc4294d6-3d60-5c9e-a862-863e1d129049" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Linear Rational Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d6501a20-6ebd-5786-870e-3527423b6332" :question/math-academy-id "e-449" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{3}{5x+2}\\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\nu=5x+2\n$$\n\nThen differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 5 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u$, solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{3}{5x + 2}dx &= 3\\int\\frac{1}{5x + 2}dx \\\\\n&= 3\\int\\frac{1}{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{5}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5}\\int\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}u & + C \\\\ = \\frac{3}{5}\\ln & 5x + 2\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063991 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdbfa506-08a1-5e43-b958-2ae373df775d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Linear Rational Function and Simplifying the Arbitrary Constant"}] :question/id #uuid "115b3fb1-1041-532a-b5fa-4d8a53c9ab2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-450" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{1+2x}\\textrm{d}x}$, writing your final answer as a single function." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\nu=1+2x\n$$\n\nThen differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u$, solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{1}{1 + 2x}dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\int\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}u & + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln & 1 + 2x\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the above by writing\n\n$$\nC = \\dfrac 1 2\\ln K\n$$\n\nfor another arbitrary constant $K > 0$, and then we can combine the two terms using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}1 + 2x & + C &= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln & 1 + 2x\\end{vmatrix}+ \\frac{1}{2}\\ln K \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln (K \\cdot \\mid 1 + 2x\\begin{vmatrix}) \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln (K \\mid 1 + 2x\\end{vmatrix})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we finally conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{1+2x}\\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac 1 2 \\ln \\left(K \\mid 1+2x \\mid \\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063992 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af32f07f-fa65-5ede-a506-735dc2d3a5ef" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Combination of Linear Rational Functions Using the General Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "2c4912bd-290a-5074-b11b-459c77b7e238" :question/math-academy-id "e-451" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\left(\\dfrac{1}{1+2x} + \\dfrac{1}{1-2x}\\right)\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(\\frac{1}{1 + 2x} + \\frac{1}{1 - 2x})dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{1 + 2x}dx + \\int\\frac{1}{1 - 2x}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}1 + 2x & -\\frac{1}{2}\\ln & 1 - 2x\\end{vmatrix}+ C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid \\frac{1 + 2x}{1 - 2x}\\begin{vmatrix}+ \\frac{1}{2}\\ln K \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln (K \\mid \\frac{1 + 2x}{1 - 2x}\\end{vmatrix})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc4294d6-3d60-5c9e-a862-863e1d129049" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Linear Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "938d9ff8-864c-5d33-b70d-b6ee6bd040aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061301} {:answer/id #uuid "b38980f8-ef07-5145-ac55-096286ecbb17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061302} {:answer/id #uuid "b62b7065-dce3-5568-97b4-f71e75f4f1ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061303} {:answer/id #uuid "049bf475-8b86-552c-86a0-91a29888bfef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061304} {:answer/id #uuid "1177d9e2-863f-5f99-953d-293bf6c24423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\ln \\mid x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b62b7065-dce3-5568-97b4-f71e75f4f1ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061303} :answer-field/id #uuid "96738ee0-5a89-513a-9fe2-ba75aebbfd4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061300}] :question/id #uuid "0fe299cc-e2f3-5032-a27f-6865f6c34c09" :question/math-academy-id "q-15707" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{2}{x + 1}dx$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af32f07f-fa65-5ede-a506-735dc2d3a5ef" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Combination of Linear Rational Functions Using the General Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba259281-257f-54f2-9ebd-235d0cb66c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\ln (K \\mid (2 + 4x)(2 - 4x) \\mid)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063245} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8e5cbe-fa70-5931-8356-41ba1621d123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\ln (K \\mid \\frac{2 + 4x}{2 - 4x} \\mid)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063246} {:answer/id #uuid "e56eec3e-6d90-5279-a5df-3bafcbbbd7fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\ln (K \\mid \\frac{2 + 4x}{2 - 4x} \\mid)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063247} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d5211b-af9e-5b7b-8f1f-61e758a489bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln (K \\mid \\frac{2 + 4x}{2 - 4x} \\mid)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063248} {:answer/id #uuid "ff606254-903e-5f32-bb04-57a169b59635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\ln (K \\mid (2 + 4x)(2 - 4x) \\mid)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf8e5cbe-fa70-5931-8356-41ba1621d123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\ln (K \\mid \\frac{2 + 4x}{2 - 4x} \\mid)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063246} :answer-field/id #uuid "11245a17-a422-5189-95c0-2d8bae5322d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063244}] :question/id #uuid "839e83ca-5b4f-5953-9460-4e14411c5b1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-49524" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int(\\frac{1}{2 + 4x} + \\frac{1}{2 - 4x})dx$."}]}
